Raye crash screen

When the kernel panics, the screen turns night violet and shows the Raye
crash picture: the eye and, set in Inter, the two sentences in English
and in French. The picture is the mono boot logo
(CONFIG_LOGO_LINUX_MONO_FILE, made by art/crash.py). Under it, in the
console font, the help address and "Stop code: " with the panic
description.

When the picture does not fit the screen, the same sentences are drawn
in the console font, French in code page 437 so the accents show. The
font is fixed: Terminus 16x32 from 1280 pixels wide, VGA 8x16 below;
the small print under the picture is always VGA 8x16.

The boot logo is off by default (fb_logo_count 0), so the eye only shows
on the crash screen; fbcon=logo-count:<n> still brings it back.

